WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.100
In rotational motion, every particle travels in a circular path centered along a fixed axis with angular velocity omega.

2
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:27.280
Torque is the rotational turning effect: tau equals r cross F, proportional to the lever arm distance r.

3
00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:42.520
Moment of inertia measures resistance to angular acceleration; mass farther from the axis creates much higher inertia.

4
00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:57.830
Placing the turning peg at the outer rim of a grinding stone maximizes lever distance r to generate high torque easily.

5
00:00:57.830 --> 00:01:16.380
When external torque is zero, angular momentum L equals I times omega and remains strictly conserved.
